# AI
# `.claude/` holds two different kinds of thing. The repo's shared agent config
# — hooks, settings, and the repo-local skills under `skills/` — is checked in
# and is what makes a session behave the same for everyone. Everything else is
# per-machine session state. Ignore the directory by default and re-include the
# shared parts, so a new skill lands in git instead of silently staying local.
.claude/*
!.claude/hooks/
!.claude/settings.json
!.claude/skills/
.claude/settings.local.json
.gemini/

# Local properties
local.properties

# Node
node_modules/

# Python (for .github/actions/lib/ scripts and their tests)
__pycache__/
*.pyc

# Daemon preview-history archive — written by the daemon's `HistoryManager` when running
# (sysprop `composeai.daemon.historyDir`). Since #3407 the default lives OUTSIDE the working
# tree, under `$XDG_CACHE_HOME/composeai/history/` — nothing new lands here. The pattern stays
# for checkouts that still carry a pre-#3407 `<moduleDir>/.compose-preview-history/`, which the
# daemon keeps using when present. Ignore at any depth.
.compose-preview-history/
